{
  "type": "user",
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
      {
        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01FHQKEbXofwJWQv65R7r1VP",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "=== list ===\nList every operation in a spec: method, path, operationId and a short\nsummary. Operations the spec did not name get a synthesised id, which is\nas callable as an authored one.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria list [spec] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help         help for list\n      --tag string   only operations carrying this tag\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== describe ===\nDescribe a single operation: its parameters, its request body and its\ndeclared responses, with every schema rendered as one compact line per\nfield rather than as raw JSON Schema.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria describe [spec] <operationId> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --depth int   how many levels of nested schema to render before truncating (default 6)\n  -h, --help        help for describe\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== search ===\nSearch a spec for a term across operation ids, paths, summaries and\ndescriptions, component schema names and parameter names. Matching is\ncase-insensitive, and results are ranked with name matches first.\n\nA term that matches nothing is not an error: an empty result set is the\nanswer that this API has no such concept.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria search [spec] <query> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help          help for search\n      --kind string   restrict results to one kind: operation|schema|param (default: all three)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== uses ===\nFind every operation that touches a schema, in a parameter, a request\nbody or a response. References are followed: an operation returning a\nPetList is reported for Pet, marked as an indirect use.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria uses [spec] <schema> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for uses\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== call ===\nBind parameters, headers and credentials to an operation and render the\nrequest as curl. Credentials are referenced by environment-variable name,\nnever by value, so the emitted command is safe to paste into a bug report\nand runnable wherever the variable is set.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria call [spec] <operationId> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --allow-mutations      permit a method other than GET, HEAD or OPTIONS\n      --body stringArray     request body: a literal, @file to read one, or - to read this process's stdin\n      --dry-run              print the curl command and send nothing\n      --fail-on-error        exit 4 if the response is an HTTP error or violates the spec\n      --header stringArray   add a request header, name=value (repeatable)\n  -h, --help                 help for call\n      --param stringArray    bind a declared parameter, name=value (repeatable)\n      --query stringArray    add a query parameter, name=value (repeatable)\n      --timeout float        give up on the request after this many seconds (default 30)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== history ===\nList the recorded request/response pairs, newest first. Everything here\nwas written redacted: a credential was never stored, so none can be read\nback. Recording is switched off per profile with `history.enabled: false`\nor everywhere with TALARIA_HISTORY=off.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria history [flags]\n  talaria history [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  replay      Re-issue a recorded call\n  show        Print one recorded request and response in full\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help               help for history\n      --operation string   only entries for this operationId\n      --since string       only entries newer than a duration ago, e.g. 1h or 30m\n      --source string      only entries from this command: call|run|replay\n      --status string      only entries with this response status: an exact code (404) or a class (4xx)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n\nUse \"talaria history [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n=== run ===\nCall every operation the filters select, check each response against the\nspec, and report one line per operation. Mutating operations are skipped\nunless --allow-mutations is given. Request data comes from the spec's own\nexamples first, then --fixtures, then generation.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria run [spec] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --allow-mutations         include operations whose method is not GET, HEAD or OPTIONS\n      --fail-on-error           exit 4 if any operation failed\n      --fixtures string         directory of <operationId>.json test data, consulted after spec examples\n  -h, --help                    help for run\n      --operation stringArray   only this operationId (repeatable); combined with --tag as a union\n      --report string           report format: json|pretty|tsv|junit (overrides --output)\n      --tag stringArray         only operations carrying this tag (repeatable)\n      --timeout float           give up on each operation's request after this many seconds (default 30)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== version ===\nPrint the talaria version\n\nUsage:\n  talaria version [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for version\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)",
        "is_error": false
      }
    ]
  },
