    "content": [
      {
        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01UwcGTE9auGd1fGaEQvmw38",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "=== auth ===\nInspect the credentials a spec's security schemes need\n\nUsage:\n  talaria auth [flags]\n  talaria auth [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  check       Report which security schemes have a credential, without reading one\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for auth\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n\nUse \"talaria auth [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n=== auth check ===\nAnswer, for each of a spec's security schemes, whether a credential is\npresent and which environment variable it comes from. Values are never\nread, so this is how an agent diagnoses a broken auth setup blind. It\nexits 5 when an operation has no credential to authenticate it with.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria auth check [spec] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for check\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== history show ===\nPrint the whole of one entry: the request as it was sent and the response\nas it came back, both redacted. Name the entry by the id `history` prints,\nwhich is stable, or by its index, which shifts every time anything is\nrecorded.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria history show <id|n> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help   help for show\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== history replay ===\nSend a recorded request again, to the URL it went to, and record the\nresult as a new entry. Credentials are resolved from the environment as\nthey were the first time — history holds their names, never their values,\nso there is nothing there to read back. Name the entry by its id: a replay\nis itself recorded, so every index shifts as soon as one runs.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria history replay <id|n> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --allow-mutations   permit replaying a method other than GET, HEAD or OPTIONS\n  -h, --help              help for replay\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)",
        "is_error": false
      }
    ]
  },
