        "text": "**33 findings: 6 CRIT, 17 WARN, 10 INFO** — committed to `REVIEW_FINDINGS.md`.\n\nAll four reviewers from `.ralph/stack.json` ran in parallel. Build, `gofmt`, `go vet` and `go test -race ./...` are clean at HEAD — every finding below is something the suite does not catch.\n\n**The six CRIT:**\n\n1. **CR/LF injection → request smuggling** (`internal/request/build.go:259`). No validation of header/cookie/method values. I reproduced this on the wire myself: one `talaria call` on a GET-only spec put a complete second `DELETE /admin HTTP/1.1` request onto the connection. Reachable from a spec's `example` value, so an untrusted API doc — the advertised workflow — defeats the `--allow-mutations` gate.\n2. **Emitted curl turns GET-with-body into POST** (`internal/curl/render.go:45`). `-X` is omitted for GET but `--data-raw` is still appended, and curl reads that as POST. The printed reproduction sends a different method than talaria did. Same class as the HEAD bug fixed in 2d92e67.\n3. **`auth check` and `call` disagree on alternative security requirements** (`internal/config/auth.go:94`). `Resolve` picks the first *supported* requirement; `satisfied` picks the first *present* one. `auth check` exits 0, `call` then exits 5 naming a variable the spec did not require.\n4. **Ctrl-C during `run` fabricates failures and exits 0** (`cmd/talaria/run.go:123`). Loop never checks `r.ctx`: 30 ops, SIGINT at 5s → report claims 28 endpoints failed that were never called, exit 0, and 1000 junk history entries can evict the previous run.\n5. **Literal `--query api_key=` leaks in cleartext via curl's stderr** (`internal/curl/exec.go:277`). `scrubber` keys on `IsSecret()` and skips sensitive *literals*, which are redacted everywhere else.\n6. **`history replay` resolves an arbitrary env var to an arbitrary host** (`cmd/talaria/history.go:668`). `ParseRef` accepts any name from the store, making the binary a \"resolve $ANY_VAR, send to $ANY_URL\" primitive.\n\nTwo things worth your attention beyond the fix loop: **Finding 23** — the e2e assertion that \"`--dry-run` equals real\" compares `Render`'s output to itself, which is why Finding 2 survived three review cycles. And **Finding 17** — 42 MB of `.ralph/*.log` agent transcripts are committed, ~403k of the diff's 433k inserted lines."
      }
