      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Committed as `b45e541`.\n\n## Plan: 6 tasks from the 6 CRIT findings\n\nOne task per finding — I checked for shared root causes and there are none; each sits in a different package with a different fix shape.\n\n| Task | Finding | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | #1 CRLF request smuggling | Reject `\\r`/`\\n` in values on all three bind paths (`located`, `pairs`, profile headers), apply `isFieldName` to spec/profile header names, validate `req.Method`, re-check in `document.auth`/`cookies` |\n| 2 | #2 GET-with-body renders as POST | Widen the `-X` guard in `render.go:45`; replace the tautological e2e assertion with one that actually executes the rendered command |\n| 3 | #3 `auth check` vs `call` disagree | Two-pass `Resolve` preferring a fully-`Present()` requirement; share one predicate with `satisfied` |\n| 4 | #4 Ctrl-C fabricates failures | Break the suite loop on cancellation, skip `recordCall`, distinct exit from `verdict` |\n| 5 | #5 Literal credential leaks via curl stderr | `scrubber` iterates `IsSensitive()`, with `Reveal()`→`Placeholder` for literals |\n| 6 | #6 replay resolves arbitrary env var | Allowlist refs to `TALARIA_AUTH_*` plus the profile's `auth:` map, reject others with exit 2 |\n\nVerification for every task is `go test ./...`, and each requires the regression test that closes its finding.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n**I verified each suggested fix rather than transcribing it.** All six hold up against the code — I read the relevant sites (`render.go:45`, `auth.go:80`/`:169`, `run.go:123`/`:403`, `exec.go:269`, `history.go:655`, `build.go:252-347`) and confirmed the fixes are coherent. Two needed sharpening: Finding 6's allowlist required threading the profile into `replayValue` (its caller already resolves one, so this is cheap), and Finding 4's suggested \"distinct error\" needed an explicit constraint that the exit code differ from both 4 and 5, since those already mean specific things.\n\n**I pulled one WARN fix into a CRIT task.** Finding 23 (the `--dry-run` e2e assertion is a tautology — it compares two outputs of the same `Render` call) is the reason Finding 2 survived three review cycles. Fixing #2 without it leaves the same blind spot, so the real e2e comparison is step 4 of Task 2. The other 16 WARN and 10 INFO findings produce no tasks, as instructed.\n\nNote that `.ralph/ralph-20260803-060103.log` is untracked and Finding 17 (WARN) flags these logs as ~42 MB of the diff — not planned, but a human should decide before the PR merges."
      }
    ],
