    "content": [
      {
        "tool_use_id": "toolu_01AzijZ8nV1cwDmnKzuanRgV",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "1\t# talaria — Review Fix Plan\n2\t\n3\tSource of truth: [docs/design/DESIGN.md](docs/design/DESIGN.md) (v0.3). Stack: `.ralph/stack.json`.\n4\tFindings: [REVIEW_FINDINGS.md](REVIEW_FINDINGS.md) — do not edit that file.\n5\t\n6\t## Scope\n7\t\n8\tThis plan replaces the previous review-fix plan, whose 9 tasks are all landed. It covers **only\n9\tthe 6 CRIT findings** (1–6) from the current review of `ralph/design` vs `main`. The 17 WARN and\n10\t10 INFO findings are deliberately **not** planned: they are recorded for a human and do not block\n11\tthe PR. Do not create work for them, and do not \"fix them while you are in the file\" — an\n12\tunrequested change in a reviewed diff costs another review cycle.\n13\t\n14\tStill out of scope, unchanged: Phases 5–8 (`internal/twin`, the recording proxy, `talaria twin …`),\n15\tdistribution and packaging, request chaining, and everything in DESIGN.md §9 Non-goals.\n16\t\n17\tEvery task lands with the regression test that proves its finding closed — a fix without one is\n18\tnot done. Build, `gofmt`, `go vet` and `go test -race ./...` are clean at HEAD and must stay so.\n19\t\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t### Task 1: Reject CR/LF in header, cookie and method values before they reach the wire\n23\t\n24\t**Fixes findings:** #1\n25\t\n26\t**Files:**\n27\t- `internal/request/build.go` (modify)\n28\t- `internal/curl/config.go` (modify)\n29\t- `internal/request/build_test.go` (modify)\n30\t- `internal/curl/config_test.go` (modify)\n31\t\n32\t**Steps:**\n33\t1. In `internal/request/build.go`, add a value check rejecting any string containing `\\r` or\n34\t   `\\n` as a usage error via `b.fail`. Apply it on every path that produces a `Pair`:\n35\t   `located` (:252, spec-declared header/cookie/query params), `pairs` (:329, the\n36\t   `--header`/`--query`/`--cookie` flags) and the profile-header branch of `headers` (:287).\n37\t   Follow the existing convention at :322-326 — report by name and position, never quote the\n38\