          "command": "git add internal/curl internal/request tasks.json IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md docs/plans && git commit -q -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix: reject CR/LF in header, cookie and method values before the wire\n\nA CR or an LF in a header name/value, a cookie name/value or the method\nends its line early on the wire and appends a header the caller never\nwrote — with a bare CRLF pair, a whole second request on the connection.\n\nTwo gates, because there are two ways a Request is born:\n\n- internal/request/build.go rejects at bind time on every path that\n  produces a Pair — spec-declared params (`located`), profile headers\n  (`headers`) and the --header/--query/--cookie flags (`pairs`). Header\n  names from the spec and from profiles are now held to isFieldName, as\n  --header names already were, and the method is held to the HTTP token\n  charset.\n- internal/curl/config.go re-checks every pair as the last gate before\n  the document. Not redundant: `history replay` rebuilds a Request from\n  a stored entry rather than from request.Build, and a credential is\n  only a string after resolve. escapeDirective is not the answer — it\n  protects curl's parser, and curl un-escapes \\r\\n back to the two\n  bytes onto the socket.\n\nRefusals are usage errors (exit 2) and never echo the offending value,\nwhich may be a credential; only names are quoted back, where %q renders\na CR or LF as an escape.\n\nFixes review finding #1 (CRIT).\nEOF\n)\" && git log --oneline -1 && git status --short"
