        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "59\t---\n60\t\n61\t### Task 2: Emit `-X GET` in the rendered curl when the request carries a body\n62\t\n63\t**Fixes findings:** #2\n64\t\n65\t**Files:**\n66\t- `internal/curl/render.go` (modify)\n67\t- `internal/curl/render_test.go` (modify)\n68\t- `internal/e2e/e2e_test.go` (modify)\n69\t\n70\t**Steps:**\n71\t1. In `internal/curl/render.go:45`, change the GET guard to\n72\t   `case req.Method != \"\" && !(strings.EqualFold(req.Method, http.MethodGet) && req.Body == nil):`\n73\t   so `-X` is emitted whenever a GET carries a body. `--data-raw` without `-X` makes curl send\n74\t   POST, while the config document at `internal/curl/config.go:149` always writes\n75\t   `request = \"GET\"` — the printed command and the executed one differ today.\n76\t2. Update the comment above the case to say why a body changes the rule: naming GET is noise\n77\t   only when curl's default method is what actually goes out.\n78\t3. Add a render test asserting `-X GET` appears for a GET-with-body, and that a bodyless GET\n79\t   still renders without `-X`.\n80\t4. Replace the tautological assertion at `internal/e2e/e2e_test.go:454` — it compares two\n81\t   outputs of the same `curl.Render` call on the same `*request.Request`, so it can never fail,\n82\t   which is why this bug survived three review cycles. Instead run the `request.curl` string\n83\t   from `--dry-run` through `sh -c` against the same `httptest` server and assert the method,\n84\t   path, headers and body the server recorded match those of the real `call`. Parameterise over\n85\t   GET-with-body, HEAD, a cookie param and a form body.\n86\t\n87\t**Verify:** `go test ./...`\n88\t- [ ] `call … --body '{\"a\":1}'` on a GET operation renders a command containing `-X GET`.\n89\t- [ ] The e2e case executes the rendered command and compares it against the server's record of\n90\t      the real call, and fails if the two methods diverge.\n91\t\n92\t---"
      }
    ]
  },
