      {
        "type": "tool_use",
        "id": "toolu_01V7CNh7a54pTUhMYmv4jh8K",
        "name": "Bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "git add internal/curl/render.go internal/curl/render_test.go internal/e2e/e2e_test.go internal/e2e/testdata/e2e-reproduce.yaml tasks.json && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -1\nfix: name GET in the rendered curl when the request carries a body\n\ncurl switches to POST for --data-raw unless -X names the method, while\nthe config document the executed call reads always writes `request =\n\"GET\"`. A GET with a body therefore printed a command that sent a\ndifferent method than the call it claimed to reproduce.\n\nThe e2e assertion that should have caught this compared two renderings of\nthe same request, so it could never fail. It now runs the command\n`--dry-run` printed through a shell against the same test server and\ncompares the method, path, headers and body the server recorded against\nthose of the real call — parameterised over a GET with a body, a HEAD, a\ncookie parameter and a form body, against a new fixture kept separate so\nthe OpenAPI 3.0 / Swagger 2.0 pair stays symmetrical.\n\nReverting the render guard makes the new case fail with\n\"method: previewed POST, call GET\".\nEOF",
          "description": "Commit the fix and tests"
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
      }
