    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Task 2 done and committed. Stopping here.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `internal/curl/render.go:45` — the GET guard is now `!(EqualFold(req.Method, GET) && req.Body == nil)`, so `-X GET` is emitted whenever a GET carries a body. Without it, `--data-raw` makes curl send POST while the config document at `internal/curl/config.go:156` always writes `request = \"GET\"`.\n- `internal/curl/render_test.go` — two unit tests: `-X GET` present for a GET-with-body, absent for a bodyless GET.\n- `internal/e2e/e2e_test.go` — replaced the tautological `called.Request.Curl != dry.Request.Curl` assertion (it compared talaria's rendering against talaria's rendering, which is why the bug survived three review cycles). A new `harness.reproduce` runs the previewed command through `sh -c` with the harness environment, and `requestDiff` compares method, path, body and the full header set as the server recorded them. Added `TestThePreviewedCommandSendsWhatTheCallSends`, parameterised over GET-with-body, HEAD, a cookie param and a form body.\n- `internal/e2e/testdata/e2e-reproduce.yaml` — new fixture for those four shapes, kept out of `e2e-api.yaml` so it stays the exact counterpart of `e2e-api-2.0.json`. All its paths are ones the existing test server already answers.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- Red confirmed on the unit test: `want it to contain -X GET`.\n- Red confirmed on the e2e test by temporarily reverting the render guard — it failed with `method: previewed POST, call GET`, then the fix was restored.\n- `go test ./...` — all 15 packages pass.\n- `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` — clean.\n\nNo doc updates needed: the `-X` rule isn't documented, and the three curl examples in README/AGENT/DESIGN are all bodyless GETs, so they still render exactly as shown."
      }
    ],
