          "command": "git add -A cmd/talaria/run.go cmd/talaria/run_test.go AGENT.md README.md tasks.json && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -1\nfix: stop a cancelled run from fabricating failures and history\n\nThe suite loop never consulted the runner's context. A Ctrl-C partway\nthrough left every remaining operation going through execute against a\ncontext that was already done: each one failed instantly, so the report\nblamed the API for requests nobody made, --fail-on-error turned that into\na validation verdict, and each one appended a SourceRun history entry —\nwhich, under trim's per-source cap, evicts the previous run's real\nhistory.\n\nThe loop now stops at the cancellation, the request that was in flight is\ndropped rather than recorded or reported, and the verdict is exit 1\nnaming how far the suite got, ahead of both the credential and the\n--fail-on-error branches: neither is a statement anyone can make about a\nsuite that did not finish.\nEOF"
        },
        "caller": {
          "type": "direct"
        }
