        "text": "Task 4 done — stopping here as required.\n\n**What changed** (`cmd/talaria/run.go`):\n\n1. **`runner.cancelled`** — new field recording that the suite's context ended mid-run.\n2. **Loop break** (`run.go:123`) — `execute`'s result is dropped and the loop stops when the runner reports cancellation, so operations after the interrupt never appear.\n3. **`execute`** — guards at the top (nothing is attempted once the context is done) and after `curl.ExecuteWith` fails on a cancelled context: `recordCall` is skipped, so no `SourceRun` history entry is written for a request that was never made.\n4. **`verdict`** — returns `clierr.RequestFailed(\"the run was cancelled after N operations\")` ahead of both the credential and `--fail-on-error` branches. Exit 1, matching a cancelled `call`; distinct from 4 and 5 without inventing a new code in the DESIGN.md §4 contract.\n\n**Test** — `TestRunCancelledPartwayReportsOnlyTheOperationsThatRan`: a server that answers the first request and, on the second, cancels the run's context and hangs until curl's connection drops. Before the fix it failed with exit 4 / `\"4 operations failed\"` — the fabricated failures exactly. Now it asserts the report covers only `listPets` and `createPet`, `summary.failed == 0`, exit 1 with a \"cancel\" message, and history holds one entry (`listPets`). Ran `-count=5` for flake; deterministic.\n\n**Verification:** `go test ./...` fully green; `test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./...` clean.\n\n**Docs:** added the interrupted-`run` behaviour to the `run` exit-code paragraph in `AGENT.md` and the interruption section of `README.md` — both already documented cancellation for `call` only.\n\nRemaining: tasks 5 and 6 are still `done: false`."
      }
    ],
