        "text": "Task 6 complete — the last open task in `tasks.json`.\n\n## What changed\n\n**The hole:** `replayValue` (cmd/talaria/history.go) turned *any* stored `<redacted:env:NAME>` back into a live `SecretRef`, and both the name and the destination URL come from `history.jsonl` — a plain file. A hand-edited entry made talaria a \"resolve `$ANY_VAR`, send it to `$ANY_URL`\" primitive, run from the one process the deployment trusts with credentials (review finding #6, CRIT).\n\n**The fix:**\n- `internal/config/auth.go` — new `(*Profile).ReferencesEnv(name)`, reusing the existing `${VAR}`/`$VAR` regexp so the profile's `auth:` map answers for itself. Nil profile and literal entries admit nothing.\n- `cmd/talaria/history.go` — new `replayableEnv` allowlist: `TALARIA_AUTH_BEARER`, `TALARIA_AUTH_BASIC`, `TALARIA_AUTH_APIKEY_*`, plus profile-named variables. Anything else is a usage error (exit 2) naming the variable and the field it stood in — not a fall-through to `request.Literal`, which would have put the `<redacted:env:NAME>` placeholder itself on the wire. The profile is threaded from the replay command through `replayRequest` → `replayQuery`/`replayPairs` → `replayValue`.\n\n**Tests (written first, failed first):** out-of-namespace refusal in headers and in the query string; all three `TALARIA_AUTH_*` forms still round-trip; a profile-named variable is accepted *and* refused when the same entry is replayed with no profile; plus an end-to-end run of the review's reproduction — seeded entry, `history replay 1` exits 2 and the test server sees no request at all. Two `internal/config` tests cover `ReferencesEnv`.\n\n**Verification:** `go test ./...` fully green (15 packages), `gofmt`/`go vet` clean. README and AGENT.md both document replay's credential behaviour and now state the allowlist and the exit-2 refusal.\n\nCommitted as `383eb98`, including the updated `tasks.json` and plan checkboxes.\n\nFinal conventions pass: all six tasks are `done: true`. I checked the three earlier commits that shipped no doc changes (`795fc18` CR/LF rejection, `b77369e` `-X GET` rendering, `fafda99` stderr scrubbing) against README/AGENT.md/DESIGN.md — none of those docs makes a claim those fixes contradict, so there was nothing to correct. Stopping here."
      }
    ],
