          "prompt": "You are the **spec-compliance** reviewer for a code review of the branch `ralph/design` against `main` in /home/casper/projects/talaria. This is a greenfield Go CLI (\"talaria\") — the entire codebase is new on this branch, so all of `cmd/` and `internal/` is in scope.\n\nDO NOT fix anything. DO NOT edit any file. Produce findings only.\n\n## Context you must read first\n- `docs/design/DESIGN.md` — THE specification. Read it in full (513 lines). Pay special attention to §3 (design principles), §4 (CLI surface, output shapes, exit codes), §5 (architecture + boundary rules), §5a (credential firewall), §7 (roadmap — the branch claims Phases 1–4).\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` and `tasks.json` — what this branch set out to do.\n- `README.md` and `AGENT.md` — the documented user/agent contract. README claims DESIGN.md is the source of truth. AGENT.md is called out in DESIGN.md §3.7 as \"a first-class deliverable ... Treat it with the same care as code\" — documentation that contradicts shipped behaviour is a real finding.\n- `git show HEAD:REVIEW_FINDINGS.md` — two prior review rounds. The 6 CRIT findings there were fixed in commits 795fc18..383eb98. **Do not re-report anything already in that file** unless you verify the fix is incomplete.\n\n## Scope\n`git diff main...HEAD` (ignore the giant `.ralph/*.log` files). Phases 1–4 are the claimed scope: `list`, `describe`, `search`, `uses`, `call` (+ `--dry-run`), `history` (+ `show`, `replay`), `run`, `auth check`, `version`. Phases 5–8 (twin, recording proxy) are explicitly NOT in scope — their absence is not a finding.\n\n## Your checklist\n- **Completeness**: is every Phase 1–4 requirement in DESIGN.md §4 and §7 actually implemented? Every flag listed in §4's CLI surface? (`--tag`, `--kind`, `--param`, `--query`, `--header`, `--body` incl. `@file` and `-`, `--base-url`, `--profile`, `--dry-run`, `--allow-mutations`, `--timeout`, `--output json|pretty|tsv`, `history --operation/--since/--status`, `run -