        "content": "talaria turns any OpenAPI/Swagger spec into an explorable API client, a\nspec-driven tester, and a digital twin — without exposing credentials to\nthe agent driving it.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria [flags]\n  talaria [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  auth        Inspect the credentials a spec's security schemes need\n  call        Build a request for one operation and show the curl that runs it\n  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell\n  describe    Show one operation's parameters, body and responses\n  help        Help about any command\n  history     List what talaria has already called and what came back\n  list        List a spec's operations, one compact line each\n  run         Smoke-test a spec's operations and report what each one did\n  search      Find operations, schemas and parameters by substring\n  uses        List the operations that reach a component schema\n  version     Print the talaria version\n\nFlags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n  -h, --help              help for talaria\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n  -v, --version           version for talaria\n\nUse \"talaria [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\n=== CALL ===\nBind parameters, headers and credentials to an operation and render the\nrequest as curl. Credentials are referenced by environment-variable name,\nnever by value, so the emitted command is safe to paste into a bug report\nand runnable wherever the variable is set.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria call [spec] <operationId> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --allow-mutations      permit a method other than GET, HEAD or OPTIONS\n      --body stringArray     request body: a literal, @file to read one, or - to read this process's stdin\n      --dry-run              print the curl command and send nothing\n      --fail-on-error        exit 4 if the response is an HTTP error or violates the spec\n      --header stringArray   add a request header, name=value (repeatable)\n  -h, --help                 help for call\n      --param stringArray    bind a declared parameter, name=value (repeatable)\n      --query stringArray    add a query parameter, name=value (repeatable)\n      --timeout float        give up on the request after this many seconds (default 30)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)\n=== RUN ===\nCall every operation the filters select, check each response against the\nspec, and report one line per operation. Mutating operations are skipped\nunless --allow-mutations is given. Request data comes from the spec's own\nexamples first, then --fixtures, then generation.\n\nUsage:\n  talaria run [spec] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --allow-mutations         include operations whose method is not GET, HEAD or OPTIONS\n      --fail-on-error           exit 4 if any operation failed\n      --fixtures string         directory of <operationId>.json test data, consulted after spec examples\n  -h, --help                    help for run\n      --operation stringArray   only this operationId (repeatable); combined with --tag as a union\n      --report string           report format: json|pretty|tsv|junit (overrides --output)\n      --tag stringArray         only operations carrying this tag (repeatable)\n      --timeout float           give up on each operation's request after this many seconds (default 30)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --base-url string   override the spec's server URL\n      --output string     output format: json|pretty|tsv (default: pretty on a terminal, json when piped)\n      --profile string    named profile from the config file: base-url + headers + auth\n      --spec string       OpenAPI/Swagger spec to use: file path or URL (default: $TALARIA_SPEC)",
        "is_error": false
      }
    ]
  },
