    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Review complete and committed as `ddb5e6a`.\n\n## 27 findings: 8 CRIT, 16 WARN, 3 INFO\n\nBaseline is healthy — build, `gofmt`, `go vet`, and `go test -race ./...` all clean (15/15 packages). All six CRIT fixes from the previous round shipped with regression tests, and three of them were re-attacked and hold.\n\n**The 8 CRIT:**\n\n1. **Credential sent to any host `--base-url` or the spec names** (`internal/request/build.go:134`) — a profile-pinned token follows `--base-url` to an attacker's listener, and a spec whose `servers[0].url` names that host is enough on its own. Directly defeats §1's core promise and isn't among §5a's three uncovered threats.\n2. **`history replay` host still unrestricted** (`cmd/talaria/history.go:560`) — commit `383eb98` closed the \"arbitrary env var\" half of the prior Finding 6; the \"arbitrary host\" half is untouched.\n3. **Parameter- and media-type-level `example`/`examples` never leave the spec loader** (`internal/operation/extract.go:166`) — `run` only sees schema-level examples, so it fires invented data at real APIs while both docs claim otherwise. Found independently by spec-compliance and integration.\n4. **OAuth2 schemes make every operation uncallable while `auth check` exits 0** (`internal/config/auth.go:225`) — §5 says \"bring your own token\" but there's no mechanism to bring one, and `run --fail-on-error` goes green having tested nothing.\n5. **Server variables in `servers[].url` never substituted** (`internal/request/build.go:158`) — a standard 3.x construct; `list` works, `call` dead-ends.\n6. **`--output tsv` structurally unsound** (`internal/output/render.go:108`) — untrusted spec text forges whole rows and varies field counts; `search` already fixes this via `collapse()`, so the inconsistency is internal.\n7. **Hostile spec `minLength`/`minItems` → runtime OOM** (`internal/gen/gen.go:178`) — dies outside `clierr` with exit 2, which tells an agent to retry forever.\n8. **Every history append rewrites the whole store under the flock** (`internal/corpus/store.go:99`) — 250x slowdown, ~2 GB RSS at the design's own retention cap, and cross-process starvation.\n\nTwo judgment calls worth flagging: I merged the duplicate example-handling and TSV findings rather than double-counting them, and I held the swallowed-signals finding at **WARN** (Finding 9) rather than CRIT — the truly unkillable case needs a pathological `curl`, while the routinely reachable one is bounded at 30 seconds. Findings 23 and 24 are prior-round WARNs re-verified as still present; since this file is regenerated each round they'd otherwise vanish."
      }
    ],
